WEBVTT

00:00:00.918 --> 00:00:04.523
Now Henry and George could
sit down to fish and potatoes.

00:00:04.523 --> 00:00:06.123
Bread and butter, too.

00:00:06.123 --> 00:00:08.854
After nearly twenty months,
all five were safe.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.637
The year before, the Invercauld
had struck the northern coast.

00:00:14.637 --> 00:00:17.862
Captain Dalgarno reckoned she
broke up in twenty minutes.

00:00:17.862 --> 00:00:20.805
Of twenty-five men,
nineteen reached the rocks.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.316
Neither crew knew of the other.

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:27.716
Smith wrote to his
wife that on calm days

00:00:27.716 --> 00:00:31.370
two men crossed to nearby islands
for seals in a boat of skins.

00:00:34.349 --> 00:00:38.118
In May a leaking ship,
the Julian, sent a boat ashore.

00:00:38.118 --> 00:00:41.293
Only George Dalgarno, Andrew Smith
and Robert Holding

00:00:41.293 --> 00:00:43.206
survived to sail with her to Callao.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.789
The Grafton’s anchors are
still there, under the water.

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:52.749
A few ribs lie in the shingle.

00:00:52.749 --> 00:00:56.660
On shore, the stones of a hearth
mark where the five made a home.

